<title>USA: Western Europe turning cooler -WSC.</title>
<headline>Western Europe turning cooler -WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Europe is trending cooler with a chance of scattered showers in the north and with the rest of the region drier and much cooler, private forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>The UK has a chance of a few showers that will favour the north. Temperatures will be below normal.</p>
<p>Germany and Central Europe will be much cooler with a chance of showers early in the period. Temperatures will be below to well below normal.</p>
<p>Southern Europe will be seasonably warm with an increasing chance of scattered showers late in the period.</p>
</text>
